      <h2 class="section-title">1. Introduction</h2>
      <p>
        Welcome to OneEarth (<strong>“Application,” “we,” “us,” “our”</strong>). We are committed to protecting your privacy and ensuring you have a positive experience on our Application. This Privacy Policy explains what information we collect, how we use it, and your rights regarding that information.
      </p>
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy applies to all users of the OneEarth mobile application and website. By downloading, installing, or using OneEarth, you agree to the terms outlined in this Privacy Policy.
      </p>

      <h2 class="section-title">2. Information We Collect</h2>

      <h3>2.1 Information You Provide Directly</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Account Information</strong>
          <ul>
            <li>Email address</li>
            <li>Username</li>
            <li>Password (encrypted)</li>
            <li>First and last name</li>
            <li>Profile picture</li>
            <li>Bio/About information</li>
            <li>Territory or location information</li>
            <li>User rank and badges</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li><strong>Communication Data</strong>
          <ul>
            <li>Messages you send through the chat feature</li>
            <li>Comments on posts</li>
            <li>Reactions to posts (likes, reactions)</li>
            <li>Notifications you receive and interact with</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li><strong>Content You Create</strong>
          <ul>
            <li>Posts you publish</li>
            <li>Comments you write</li>
            <li>Reactions you give</li>
            <li>Profile information you share</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li><strong>Payment Information</strong>
          <ul>
            <li>If applicable, payment method details for in-app purchases (processed securely by third-party payment providers)</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>2.2 Information Collected Automatically</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Device Information</strong>
          <ul>
            <li>Device model and manufacturer</li>
            <li>Operating system and version</li>
            <li>Android version</li>
            <li>Device ID</li>
            <li>IDFA (Identifier for Advertising) where applicable</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li><strong>Firebase &amp; Analytics Data</strong>
          <ul>
            <li>Firebase Analytics events</li>
            <li>User interaction events</li>
            <li>App crash reports</li>
            <li>App performance metrics</li>
            <li>Session duration</li>
            <li>Feature usage statistics</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li><strong>Firebase Cloud Messaging (FCM)</strong>
          <ul>
            <li>FCM registration token (used to send push notifications)</li>
            <li>Push notification delivery status</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li><strong>Location Information</strong>
          <ul>
            <li>Territory/region selected by user (if provided)</li>
            <li>Approximate location derived from user profile</li>
            <li>NOT precise GPS location (unless explicitly granted)</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li><strong>Network Information</strong>
          <ul>
            <li>IP address</li>
            <li>Internet service provider (ISP)</li>
            <li>Connection type (WiFi, mobile data)</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li><strong>Log Data</strong>
          <ul>
            <li>Timestamps of app usage</li>
            <li>Features accessed</li>
            <li>API requests made</li>
            <li>Error logs</li>
            <li>Performance metrics</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>2.3 Information from Third Parties</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Firebase Services</strong>
          <ul>
            <li>Google Firebase provides analytics and authentication services</li>
            <li>Data from Firebase services as specified in Google's privacy policy</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li><strong>Social Integrations</strong>
          <ul>
            <li>If you sign in via social accounts, we may receive profile information (subject to your privacy settings on that platform)</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="section-title">3. How We Use Your Information</h2>

      <h3>3.1 Core Service Delivery</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Creating and maintaining your account</li>
        <li>Enabling you to post content and interact with other users</li>
        <li>Processing messages and chat communications</li>
        <li>Displaying your profile and content to other users</li>
        <li>Managing user rankings and badges</li>
        <li>Electoral features (elections, voting, nominations)</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>3.2 Push Notifications</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Sending you notifications for:
          <ul>
            <li>New messages</li>
            <li>Reactions to your posts</li>
            <li>Comments on your posts</li>
            <li>Friend requests</li>
            <li>Electoral notifications</li>
            <li>Profile views</li>
            <li>App updates</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>3.3 Analytics &amp; Improvement</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Understanding how users interact with the app</li>
        <li>Improving app performance and stability</li>
        <li>Debugging and fixing errors</li>
        <li>Developing new features</li>
        <li>Optimizing user experience</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>3.4 Communication</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Sending service announcements</li>
        <li>Responding to your inquiries</li>
        <li>Providing customer support</li>
        <li>Notifying you of policy changes</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>3.5 Security &amp; Safety</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Detecting and preventing fraud</li>
        <li>Protecting against malicious activity</li>
        <li>Enforcing our Terms of Service</li>
        <li>Protecting user safety and rights</li>
        <li>Investigating abuse and violations</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>3.6 Legal Compliance</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Complying with legal obligations</li>
        <li>Responding to lawful requests from authorities</li>
        <li>Protecting our legal rights</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="section-title">4. Data Sharing &amp; Disclosure</h2>

      <h3>4.1 Information We Do NOT Share</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>We <strong>do NOT sell</strong> your personal data to third parties for marketing purposes.</li>
        <li>We <strong>do NOT</strong> share your password with anyone.</li>
        <li>We <strong>do NOT</strong> share your precise location (unless explicitly requested for a feature).</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>4.2 Information We DO Share</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Public Content</strong>
          <ul>
            <li>Your posts, comments, and reactions are visible to other users as part of the social experience</li>
            <li>Your profile information (name, username, rank, badges) is visible to other users</li>
            <li>This is intentional to enable social networking</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li><strong>With Service Providers</strong>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Firebase</strong> (Google) - for authentication, analytics, cloud messaging, and data storage</li>
            <li><strong>Payment Processors</strong> - if you make purchases, payment information is shared with PCI-compliant processors</li>
            <li><strong>Cloud Storage Providers</strong> - for storing user data securely</li>
            <li>These providers are contractually obligated to protect your data</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li><strong>Legal Requirements</strong>
          <ul>
            <li>Law enforcement, government agencies, or court orders requiring disclosure</li>
            <li>Protection of rights, privacy, or safety of users or the public</li>
            <li>Enforcement of our Terms of Service</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li><strong>With Your Consent</strong>
          <ul>
            <li>Any other sharing you explicitly authorize</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>4.3 Data Retention Partners</h3>
      <div class="fineprint">Partner | Purpose | Privacy Policy</div>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Google Firebase</strong> — Authentication, Storage, Analytics, Messaging — <span class="mono">https://policies.google.com/privacy</span></li>
        <li><strong>Firebase Cloud Messaging (FCM)</strong> — Push Notifications — <span class="mono">https://policies.google.com/privacy</span></li>
        <li><strong>Firebase Analytics</strong> — Usage Analytics — <span class="mono">https://policies.google.com/privacy</span></li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="section-title">5. Data Storage &amp; Security</h2>

      <h3>5.1 Data Storage Location</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>User data is stored in <strong>Google Cloud Firestore</strong> (secure cloud database)</li>
        <li>Data is encrypted at rest and in transit</li>
        <li>Backup copies may be maintained for disaster recovery</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>5.2 Security Measures</h3>
      <p>We implement industry-standard security measures:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Encryption</strong>: Data encrypted in transit (TLS/SSL) and at rest</li>
        <li><strong>Authentication</strong>: Secure password storage with encryption</li>
        <li><strong>Access Control</strong>: Limited employee access to user data</li>
        <li><strong>Firewalls</strong>: Network security protections</li>
        <li><strong>Regular Audits</strong>: Security assessments and testing</li>
        <li><strong>Secure APIs</strong>: HTTPS-only communication</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>5.3 Limitations</h3>
      <p>
        No security system is 100% secure. While we use reasonable security measures, we cannot guarantee absolute security. Users are responsible for protecting their login credentials.
      </p>

      <h3>5.4 Data Breach Notification</h3>
      <p>
        In the unlikely event of a data breach, we will:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Notify affected users without unreasonable delay</li>
        <li>Cooperate with relevant authorities</li>
        <li>Implement remedial measures</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="section-title">6. Your Privacy Rights</h2>

      <h3>6.1 Access Your Data</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>You have the right to:</li>
        <li>Access your personal data stored in our system</li>
        <li>Request a copy of your data</li>
        <li>Review your profile information at any time</li>
      </ul>
      <p>To request access: <span class="mono">privacy@oneearth.app</span></p>

      <h3>6.2 Correct Your Data</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>You can edit your profile information in the app</li>
        <li>Update your email address</li>
        <li>Change your password</li>
        <li>Modify your preferences</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>6.3 Delete Your Account</h3>
      <p>
        You have the right to delete your account and associated data, including requesting permanent removal of your content.
      </p>
      <p><strong>Account Deletion Process</strong>:</p>
      <ol>
        <li>Go to Settings in the app</li>
        <li>Select "Delete Account"</li>
        <li>Confirm deletion</li>
        <li>Your account and associated personal data will be deleted within 30 days</li>
        <li>Some aggregated data may be retained for statistical purposes</li>
      </ol>

      <h3>6.4 Export Your Data</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>You can request your data in a portable format via:</li>
        <li>Email: <span class="mono">privacy@oneearth.app</span></li>
        <li>We will provide data within 30 days</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>6.5 Opt-Out Rights</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Push Notifications</strong>: Disable in app Settings or device settings</li>
        <li><strong>Analytics Tracking</strong>: Opt out in Settings (may limit app functionality)</li>
        <li><strong>Marketing Communications</strong>: Unsubscribe from emails (we don't send unsolicited marketing)</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>6.6 Do Not Track</h3>
      <p>
        Some browsers include "Do Not Track" features. We currently do not respond to DNT signals, but you can control tracking through device settings and app preferences.
      </p>

      <h2 class="section-title">7. Children's Privacy</h2>

      <h3>7.1 Age Restriction</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>OneEarth is intended for users <strong>13 years of age and older</strong> (or the minimum age required in your jurisdiction).</li>
        <li>We <strong>do not knowingly collect</strong> personal information from children under 13.</li>
        <li>If we become aware that we've collected data from someone under 13, we will delete that information immediately and cease collecting data from that user.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>7.2 Parental Controls</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Parents or guardians of minors using this app should review this Privacy Policy</li>
        <li>Monitor their child's account activity</li>
        <li>Use device-level parental controls available in Android settings</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>7.3 Children Under 13</h3>
      <p>If you're a parent or guardian and believe we've collected information from a child under 13, please contact us immediately: <span class="mono">privacy@oneearth.app</span></p>

      <h2 class="section-title">8. California Privacy Rights (CCPA)</h2>
      <p>
        If you're a California resident, you have additional rights under the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA):
      </p>

      <h3>8.1 Right to Know</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>You can request what personal information we collect, use, share</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>8.2 Right to Delete</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>You can request deletion of personal information (with exceptions)</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>8.3 Right to Opt-Out</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>You can opt out of "sales" of personal data (we don't sell data for marketing)</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>8.4 Right to Non-Discrimination</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>You won't face discrimination for exercising CCPA rights</li>
      </ul>

      <p><strong>To Exercise CCPA Rights</strong>: Email <span class="mono">privacy@oneearth.app</span> with your full name, email address, and specific request (know, delete, opt-out). We'll verify your identity and respond within 45 days.</p>

      <h2 class="section-title">9. European Privacy Rights (GDPR)</h2>
      <p>If you're in the European Union or United Kingdom, you have rights under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR):</p>

      <h3>9.1 Legal Basis for Processing</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Consent</strong> - Your agreement to this Privacy Policy</li>
        <li><strong>Contract</strong> - Necessary to provide services</li>
        <li><strong>Legal Obligation</strong> - Compliance with laws</li>
        <li><strong>Legitimate Interests</strong> - Improving services and security</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>9.2 GDPR Rights</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Right of Access: Request copy of your data</li>
        <li>Right to Rectification: Correct inaccurate data</li>
        <li>Right to Erasure: Delete your data ("right to be forgotten")</li>
        <li>Right to Restrict Processing: Limit how data is used</li>
        <li>Right to Data Portability: Receive data in portable format</li>
        <li>Right to Object: Oppose certain processing</li>
        <li>Right to Lodge a Complaint: Contact your Data Protection Authority</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>9.3 Data Controller &amp; DPO</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Data Controller</strong>: OneEarth Inc.</li>
        <li><strong>Data Protection Officer</strong>: <span class="mono">privacy@oneearth.app</span></li>
        <li><strong>Your Data Protection Authority</strong>: Contact the DPA in your country for complaints</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="section-title">10. Cookies &amp; Tracking Technologies</h2>

      <h3>10.1 Cookies in Web Version</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Session Cookies</strong>: Necessary for login and functionality</li>
        <li><strong>Persistent Cookies</strong>: Remember preferences</li>
        <li><strong>Analytics Cookies</strong>: Track usage patterns</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>10.2 Third-Party Tracking</h3>
      <p>
        Google Analytics may track pages visited, time spent on pages, traffic sources, and user interactions.
      </p>
      <p>You can opt out of Google Analytics at: <span class="mono">https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout</span></p>

      <h3>10.3 Mobile App Tracking</h3>
      <p>The mobile app uses Firebase Analytics, crash reporting, and performance monitoring.</p>
      <p>You can disable analytics in app Settings.</p>

      <h3>10.4 Disabling Cookies</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Browser</strong>: Visit browser settings to disable cookies</li>
        <li><strong>Mobile App</strong>: Go to Settings > Privacy > Disable Analytics</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="section-title">11. Third-Party Links &amp; Services</h2>
      <p>
        OneEarth may contain links to third-party websites or services. This Privacy Policy applies only to OneEarth. When you use third-party services, their privacy policies apply.
      </p>
      <p>
        We recommend reviewing their privacy policies before sharing information.
      </p>

      <h2 class="section-title">12. International Data Transfers</h2>
      <p>
        Your data may be transferred to, stored in, and processed in countries other than your country of residence. These countries may have different data protection laws.
      </p>
      <p>
        By using OneEarth, you consent to data transfers to countries where we operate and processing of data outside your home country.
      </p>
      <p>
        Data transfers to the US are made under appropriate safeguards (Standard Contractual Clauses, etc.).
      </p>

      <h2 class="section-title">13. Policy Updates</h2>

      <h3>13.1 Changes to This Policy</h3>
      <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy at any time to reflect changes in our practices, comply with new laws, or improve clarity.
      </p>

      <h3>13.2 Notification of Changes</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Major changes will be posted at: <span class="mono">https://oneearth.app/privacy</span></li>
        <li>You'll be notified via in-app notification, email (for material changes), and the updated "Last Updated" date</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>13.3 Your Continued Use</h3>
      <p>
        Continued use of the app after policy changes means you accept the new terms. For material changes, we'll request explicit consent before enforcement.
      </p>

      <h2 class="section-title">14. Contact Us</h2>
      <p>If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or our privacy practices:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Email</strong>: <span class="mono">privacy@oneearth.app</span></li>
        <li><strong>Website</strong>: <span class="mono">https://oneearth.app</span></li>
      </ul>
      <p class="fineprint">We aim to respond to privacy inquiries within 14 business days.</p>

      <h2 class="section-title">15. Data Protection Authority</h2>
      <p>If you believe we've violated your privacy rights and wish to make a formal complaint:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>United States (FTC)</strong>: https://reportfraud.ftc.gov</li>
        <li><strong>European Union (GDPR)</strong>: https://edpb.ec.europa.eu/about-edpb/board/members_en</li>
        <li><strong>United Kingdom (ICO)</strong>: https://ico.org.uk</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="section-title">16. Supplementary Provisions</h2>

      <h3>16.1 Do We Sell Data?</h3>
      <p><strong>No.</strong> We do not sell personal data to advertisers or third parties for marketing purposes.</p>

      <h3>16.2 Automated Decision-Making</h3>
      <p>We may use automated systems for spam detection, fraud detection, content moderation, and user ranking algorithms. You have the right to request human review and opt out where legally possible.</p>

      <h3>16.3 Accessibility</h3>
      <p>This Privacy Policy is available in English (primary) and [Other languages as applicable]. For accessibility assistance: <span class="mono">accessibility@oneearth.app</span></p>

      <h3>16.4 Biometric Data</h3>
      <p>OneEarth does not collect or process biometric data except as provided by your device's built-in authentication (which we don't access directly).</p>

      <h2 class="section-title">17. Glossary of Terms</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Personal Data</strong>: Information that identifies or relates to an individual</li>
        <li><strong>Processing</strong>: Any action taken with personal data (collection, storage, use, sharing, deletion)</li>
        <li><strong>Consent</strong>: Explicit, informed agreement to data processing</li>
        <li><strong>FCM Token</strong>: Unique identifier for push notification delivery via Firebase Cloud Messaging</li>
        <li><strong>Firestore</strong>: Google's cloud database used to store app data</li>
        <li><strong>GDPR</strong>: General Data Protection Regulation (EU privacy law)</li>
        <li><strong>CCPA</strong>: California Consumer Privacy Act (California privacy law)</li>
        <li><strong>Recipient</strong>: Person receiving a message or notification</li>
        <li><strong>Sender</strong>: Person sending a message</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="section-title">18. Acknowledgment</h2>
      <p>
        By using the OneEarth application, you acknowledge that you have read, understood, and agree to this Privacy Policy. If you do not agree with any part of this policy, please discontinue use of the application and delete it from your device.
      </p>

